WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.403 --> 00:00:01.243
- Welcome back.

00:00:01.243 --> 00:00:02.430
Sometimes on this show,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:04.230
a theme will come up in our interviews,

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.740
a running topic that
emerges over and over again.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.500
Somehow last season ghost
stories became a running theme

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.470
which is terrifying to me,
cuz not really into that.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.140
And here's a mash up of some of the best.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.180
I heard that you had a scary ghost story.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.140
- I do I do.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.940
- I love anything that's like paranormal

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.130
and weird and unexplained.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.510
- You're originally from
New Hampshire, right?

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.343
- I am.

00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:26.646
- Is anything haunted where
you're from everything.

00:00:26.646 --> 00:00:28.110
- Every thing, every single thing.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.100
- I'm the first one to say that

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.480
what I do is absolutely crazy.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.580
How can someone communicate
with someone that has died?

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.600
- People have died everywhere.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.433
If they're a ghost.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:35.670
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:36.900
- They're gonna be kind of around.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.943
- Oh, come on. I can't, I can't.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.730
- I got you Kelly.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.352
- Oh my God.

00:00:43.352 --> 00:00:44.185
(crowd cheering)

00:00:44.185 --> 00:00:45.480
- True or false.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.763
There are ghosts in the white house.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.740
- True.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.179
- Never going

00:00:51.179 --> 00:00:53.640
- True and listen, Kelly, you
would've liked these ghosts

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.830
cuz they were very musical.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.650
They were musical and came with no harm.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.320
They were kind, friendly,
compassionate ghosts.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.420
So Barbara and I were going to sleep,

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.460
our rooms were right next to each other

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.560
and it was in college when
people would call late.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.230
So our phone rang and I woke up

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:14.460
and all of a sudden we
heard 1920s piano music

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.830
coming out of our fireplace.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.170
And I was like, surely that's
like the cat or something.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.160
You know, we had to pretend.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.690
But it was the middle of the night.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.050
And you could feel the
music outta the fireplace.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.060
And I know we tried to talk
ourselves out of it too.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.350
Like I can see you.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.790
What do you think?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.623
- What I think is,

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.104
I would've immediately
exited the premises.

00:01:33.104 --> 00:01:34.170
Oh my God.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.000
Is it true that you have
a new passion in life?

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.110
Are you obsessed with ghosts?

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.345
I hear you are.

00:01:38.345 --> 00:01:39.210
- It's not really a new passion.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:40.410
- Okay. We are just finding out.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.090
- You're just kind of like finding out.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.287
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:43.287 --> 00:01:45.090
- Yeah. I feel like I have,
I've accepted the fact

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:49.710
that like I see things
and I hear things and

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.560
- [Kelly] Wait do you really,
you've had like experiences?

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.350
- Yeah, a lot of them, a
lot of them over the years,

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.590
like even as a child growing
up, like I remember being,

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:00.900
like getting ready for school
when I was eight years old.

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.640
And there was you know those ducks.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.460
That like, is like the duck
thing that you pull to toy.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.293
- Yeah.

00:02:06.293 --> 00:02:07.710
- There was one of those
on the dining room table,

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:08.543
and I started walking

00:02:08.543 --> 00:02:10.290
and it just started
like going alongside me.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.813
And I was like interesting,

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.720
and I kind of shut it down for a while

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.800
because like it's scary.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.700
But I recently was like,
no, this is like a gift

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.240
and like something that
I have ability to do.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.350
So I'm gonna lean into it.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.480
And I recently did my first like

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.260
real paranormal investigation
with equipment and everything.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.690
- What equipment, like
what kind of equipment?

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:36.480
- There's a lot, so much
on the market genuinely.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.348
- What?

00:02:37.348 --> 00:02:39.120
- But like my favorite thing
is called a spirit box.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.950
- Okay. If you were a ghost

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.100
do you think you'd wanna,
I would follow people.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.360
I would follow people.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.683
I'd just be nosy.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.660
- And I was little, my
best friend and Pia.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.400
She was there obviously.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.800
And we were about four and six

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.590
and we were taking a bath
in the bathtub playing

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.920
and a shirt flew in, arms outstretched.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.230
Pia, you know this, wherever Pia is.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.200
arms outstretched, hovered
over the little tub

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.033
and then it fell in.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:10.890
And whatever you're four
and six it's not that scary.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.240
But when I

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.830
- What? That is scary at four and six.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.900
- But not when you are little.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.130
you're like, I don't know.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.810
Or maybe we weren't that bright..

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.580
- Or maybe you were just,
may be you were just like,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:21.810
is that supposed to happen?

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.355
Wait, oh my gosh.

00:03:23.355 --> 00:03:24.188
- I think we weren't there.

00:03:24.188 --> 00:03:25.021
I'm I'm looking back.

00:03:25.021 --> 00:03:25.854
I'm scared now

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:31.530
- When I was probably about
seven or eight years old,

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:32.950
we lived in a house here

00:03:34.355 --> 00:03:36.810
and all these kind of
weird things would go on

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.470
and they would be kind of
innocuous in the beginning

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.780
like little taps on the windows
in the middle of the night

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.450
when there was nothing
near the window to tap it.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.520
So you just kind of hear a click.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.350
And then I was in the bathtub

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.930
and my mom's bathtub
and she was bathing me

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.990
and I looked up and there
was no air or anything.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.360
And there was a chandelier by the bathtub,

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.430
a little boat and it was just going

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.730
left to right to left
to right outta nowhere.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.670
And then it just stopped the
minute that I noticed it.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.503
And then.

00:04:06.503 --> 00:04:07.670
- [Kelly] Did you mom see it?

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:08.503
- Weird stuff kept happening.

00:04:08.503 --> 00:04:09.336
Yeah.

00:04:09.336 --> 00:04:10.169
- [Kelly] Did your mom see it?

00:04:10.169 --> 00:04:11.002
- Yeah my mom saw it.

00:04:11.002 --> 00:04:11.835
- I would've grabbed you and run.

00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:13.113
- In, yeah, literally.

